      "title_align": "left",
      "section": "Volume nuclei",
      "order": 3,
      "alignment": "left",
      "vertical_alignment": "top",
      "body": "Eight planes of a kidney volume (2.5 um apart) in two channels, over five timepoints. The time course is synthetic: each frame is the same volume seen through a window that drifts a few pixels and loses 8 % of its signal, as a bleaching acquisition would. Use the z and t sliders of the viewer. The points are the nuclei of the first timepoint, segmented in 3D; the depth filter keeps the upper, middle or lower third.\n",
      "wf_tag": "python/bioimage_demo"
    },
